# Who reviews what.
#
# The layout is what makes this file short: a feature is one directory, so a team
# owns a line rather than a list of files scattered across services/, requests/
# and repo/.
#
# GitHub reads this from the repository root, .github/ or docs/. The owners
# below are placeholders (@platform, @team-orders): replace them with real users
# or teams, then uncomment the rules. GitHub flags an unknown owner as an error
# in this file, which is why they start out commented.

# --- Shared kernel and wiring -------------------------------------------------
# Everything depends on these, so a change here can break any team's module. They
# also encode the rules the layout rests on, which is why they are not owned by
# whoever happened to need them changed.
# /models/                @platform
# /consts/
# /middlewares/
# /repo/
# /emsgs/
# /testkit/               @platform
# /arch/                  @platform
# /cmd/                   @platform
# /prisma/                @platform
# /.github/               @platform
# /.golangci.yml          @platform
# /Makefile               @platform

# --- Modules ------------------------------------------------------------------
# One line per module — the trailing slash covers handler/, service/, store/ and
# anything added later. A team owns its module, plus the three files elsewhere
# that belong to it: the model, the schema, and its error codes.
#
#   /modules/orders/            @team-orders
#   /models/order.model.go      @team-orders
#   /prisma/schema/orders.prisma @team-orders
#   /emsgs/order.emsgs.go       @team-orders
#
# The model and schema lines override the shared-kernel rule above, because a
# later match wins. That is deliberate: a table's shape is the owning team's to
# change, while the package it sits in is the platform's to keep coherent.

# /modules/auth/          @platform
# /models/access_token.model.go @platform
# /emsgs/auth.emsgs.go    @platform

# /modules/user/          @platform
# /models/user.model.go   @platform
# /emsgs/user.emsgs.go    @platform

# /modules/note/          @platform
# /models/note.model.go   @platform
# /emsgs/note.emsgs.go    @platform
